# Data Model

Every table includes: `id uuid pk default gen_random_uuid()`, `created_at timestamptz default now()`, `updated_at timestamptz default now()`, `updated_by` (references auth.users, nullable while single-user).

## 1. Kitchen inventory (`kitchen_inventory`)
- item_name text
- category text
- unit text (kg, litre, pack, etc.)
- current_qty numeric
- reorder_level numeric
- reorder_qty numeric
- supplier text
- cost_per_unit numeric
- last_restocked_at date
- notes text

Derived state: `status = current_qty <= reorder_level ? 'low' : 'ok'` — computed, not stored.

## 2. IT equipment register (`it_equipment`)
- asset_tag text unique
- item_name text
- category text (laptop, monitor, router, printer, etc.)
- assigned_to text
- serial_number text
- purchase_date date
- warranty_expiry date
- status text (active, in_repair, retired)
- location text
- notes text
- warranty_card_url text (Supabase Storage path — warranty card photo/PDF)

## 2b. Appliances register (`appliances`)
Same shape as IT equipment (asset tag, name, category, assignment, serial, purchase/warranty dates, status, location, notes) plus:
- warranty_card_url text (Supabase Storage path — warranty card photo/PDF)

Categories are site appliances (AC, fridge, microwave, etc.). One warranty card file per item. Uploads go to the `warranty-cards` bucket (dashboard only; the chat agent cannot attach files).

## 3. Generator (`generator_maintenance`, `generator_fuel_log`)
`generator_maintenance`:
- service_date date
- next_service_due date (default: service_date + 1 month — monthly checkup cadence)
- service_type text
- vendor text
- cost numeric
- notes text
- checkup_status text (`done` | `not_done`) — whether this checkup was completed

`generator_fuel_log`:
- log_date date
- liters_added numeric
- running_hours numeric
- fuel_level_pct numeric
- cost numeric
- notes text

`generator_expenses` (ledger / fuel expense sheets):
- expense_date date
- account text
- description text
- debit numeric (summed for total expense)
- credit numeric (optional)
- notes text

Site date display/parse convention: DD/MM/YYYY (stored as ISO dates).

## 4. Solar system (`solar_specs`, `solar_monitoring_log`)
`solar_specs` (effectively one row, but keep as a table for history):
- panel_capacity_kw numeric
- inverter_model text
- battery_capacity_kwh numeric
- install_date date
- vendor text
- warranty_expiry date
- spec_file_url text (Supabase Storage path — original Word/PDF)

`solar_monitoring_log`:
- log_date date
- generation_kwh numeric
- consumption_kwh numeric
- battery_soc_pct numeric
- alert_flag boolean default false
- notes text

## 5. Internet & utility accounts (`utility_accounts`)
- utility_type text (internet, electricity, gas, water)
- provider text
- account_number text
- billing_cycle text
- monthly_avg_cost numeric
- due_date_day int (day of month bill is due)
- contact_person text
- notes text
- **never store passwords/credentials in this table or anywhere in the app.** Reference a password manager entry name only.

## 6. Tenants (`tenants`, `tenant_rent_logs`, `tenant_electric_bills`)
`tenants` (account + current rent snapshot):
- tenant_name text (unique, case-insensitive)
- rent_amount numeric
- rent_due_date date
- payment_status text (`paid` | `unpaid` | `partial` | `overdue`)
- payment_date date
- outstanding_amount numeric
- notes text

`tenant_rent_logs` (history per tenant; latest log syncs the tenant snapshot):
- tenant_id uuid → tenants
- same rent/payment fields as the tenant snapshot

`tenant_electric_bills` (K-Electric charges billed to the tenant — not site utility meters):
- tenant_id uuid → tenants
- ke_charges_amount numeric
- due_date date
- payment_status text (`paid` | `unpaid` | `partial` | `overdue`)
- payment_date date
- outstanding_amount numeric
- notes text

## 7. Chart of Accounts (`chart_of_accounts_entries`)
Subsidiary ledgers (one table, `ledger` discriminator):
- ledger text — `solar_panel_clifton` | `eobi` | `k_electric_gondpass` | `kwsb_clifton`
- entry_date date
- ref_no text (e.g. CPV-74, J-511)
- account_description text (Accounts / Description column)
- document_no text (Document # / narration)
- debit numeric default 0
- credit numeric default 0
- notes text

Derived: running balance = prior balance + debit − credit (computed in UI / agent, not stored).

## Adding a new domain later
Follow the same shape: base audit columns + domain fields + one `..._log` table if the domain has recurring events (like fuel or monitoring). Don't invent a different pattern.
